WEBVTT

1
00:00:34.375 --> 00:00:41.000
<b>Arjuna had asked some questions about the Sthita</b>
<b>-Prajna,meaning a person of unwavering intellect.</b>

2
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.791
<b>His first question was</b>

3
00:00:42.791 --> 00:00:46.333
<b>what are the special </b>
<b>characteristics of such a person?</b>

4
00:00:46.333 --> 00:00:49.333
<b>Here, Krishna is answering that.</b>

5
00:00:49.333 --> 00:00:50.625
<b>He says</b>

6
00:00:50.625 --> 00:00:52.666
<b>a Sthita-Prajna is one</b>

7
00:00:52.666 --> 00:00:56.541
<b>who renounces all desires of the mind</b>

8
00:00:56.541 --> 00:01:01.458
<b>and finds contentment in self-realization alone.</b>

9
00:01:06.416 --> 00:01:07.458
<b>A Sthita-Prajna</b>

10
00:01:07.458 --> 00:01:11.791
<b>or person of unwavering intellect</b>
<b>is one whose mind is pure.</b>

11
00:01:11.791 --> 00:01:13.958
<b>Pure mind means:</b>

12
00:01:13.958 --> 00:01:18.833
<b>When the mind is free from </b>
<b>desires for sensory pleasures</b>

13
00:01:18.833 --> 00:01:23.208
<b>or the enjoyment they create</b>

14
00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:26.666
<b>And when the mind finds satisfaction </b>
<b>only in activities related to self-realization,</b>

15
00:01:26.666 --> 00:01:31.208
<b>meaning activities connected to the soul</b>

16
00:01:31.208 --> 00:01:32.208
<b>But</b>

17
00:01:32.208 --> 00:01:36.708
<b>where do these cravings for</b>
<b>pleasure and enjoyment come from?</b>

18
00:01:36.708 --> 00:01:39.666
<b>Krishna indicates this here.</b>

19
00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:41.916
<b>In the Sanskrit pronunciation of this verse,</b>

20
00:01:41.916 --> 00:01:43.333
<b>there's a word</b>

21
00:01:43.333 --> 00:01:45.000
<b>'Manogataan',</b>

22
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.666
<b>meaning the wandering of the mind.</b>

23
00:01:48.666 --> 00:01:50.666
<b>Our mind keeps wandering,</b>

24
00:01:50.666 --> 00:01:55.708
<b>seeking new pleasures, </b>
<b>and from there desires arise.</b>

25
00:01:55.708 --> 00:01:57.208
<b>For example</b>

26
00:01:57.208 --> 00:02:00.208
<b>when you taste some delicious food,</b>

27
00:02:00.208 --> 00:02:02.291
<b>it pleases the mind,</b>

28
00:02:02.291 --> 00:02:07.250
<b>the mind starts desiring it, </b>
<b>feels this is the source of joy,</b>

29
00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:09.333
<b>from here craving arises,</b>

30
00:02:09.333 --> 00:02:14.791
<b>and now the mind wanders in pursuit </b>
<b>of finding something tasty to eat.</b>

31
00:02:14.791 --> 00:02:18.166
<b>When senses come in contact with objects,</b>

32
00:02:18.166 --> 00:02:21.333
<b>their experiences transmit to the mind,</b>

33
00:02:21.333 --> 00:02:22.708
<b>and in response,</b>

34
00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:25.666
<b>the mind generates desires.</b>

35
00:02:25.666 --> 00:02:31.750
<b>This is why sages traditionally </b>
<b>meditate in distant mountains.</b>

36
00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:36.041
<b>In remote mountains, </b>
<b>senses contact fewer objects,</b>

37
00:02:36.041 --> 00:02:39.458
<b>which helps in controlling the mind.</b>

38
00:02:39.458 --> 00:02:40.458
<b>But</b>

39
00:02:40.458 --> 00:02:43.958
<b>can anyone live without desires?</b>

40
00:02:43.958 --> 00:02:47.958
<b>Won't life become bland without desires?</b>

41
00:02:47.958 --> 00:02:50.000
<b>What about life's joy?</b>

42
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.250
<b>A person of steady wisdom certainly stops</b>
<b>the mind's wandering,</b>

43
00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:56.583
<b>certainly controls cravings,</b>

44
00:02:56.583 --> 00:02:59.583
<b>but desires still remain.</b>

45
00:02:59.583 --> 00:03:04.625
<b>The only difference is that these </b>
<b>desires become spiritual.</b>

46
00:03:04.625 --> 00:03:07.625
<b>They find joy in spirituality alone.</b>

47
00:03:07.625 --> 00:03:12.625
<b>This means that such a person </b>
<b>now engages in all activities</b>

48
00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:17.875
<b>that help them understand their </b>
<b>spiritual truth more deeply,</b>

49
00:03:17.875 --> 00:03:21.291
<b>strengthen their connection with the Divine.</b>

50
00:03:21.291 --> 00:03:22.291
<b>Meditation,</b>

51
00:03:22.291 --> 00:03:23.416
<b>prayer,</b>

52
00:03:23.416 --> 00:03:24.416
<b>service,</b>

53
00:03:24.416 --> 00:03:25.750
<b>self-reflection</b>

54
00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:30.291
<b>all these become their path to contentment.</b>

55
00:03:35.291 --> 00:03:39.750
<b>Today there's an invitation for a feast,</b>

56
00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:44.500
<b>how joyful it will be to taste delicious dishes!</b>

57
00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:49.500
<b>That attire looks so beautiful on that person.</b>

58
00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:52.333
<b>It would look great on me too.</b>

59
00:03:52.333 --> 00:03:56.166
<b>Have seen/heard so much about this thing,</b>

60
00:03:56.166 --> 00:03:59.000
<b>if only I could get it.</b>

61
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.333
<b>Haha... </b>

62
00:04:00.333 --> 00:04:02.958
<b>countless thoughts of the mind.</b>

63
00:04:02.958 --> 00:04:06.541
<b>You experience these too, don't you?</b>

64
00:04:06.541 --> 00:04:13.375
<b>Mental images of alluring </b>
<b>objects, people, situations.</b>

65
00:04:13.375 --> 00:04:18.083
<b>Seeing something with someone else, </b>
<b>desiring to possess it.</b>

66
00:04:18.083 --> 00:04:19.625
<b>And then</b>

67
00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:24.000
<b>when encountering that object/person,</b>

68
00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:35.208
<b>often realizing reality was quite</b>
<b>different from the mind's image.</b>

69
00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:40.166
<b>Then the mind getting attracted to a new image. </b>

70
00:04:40.166 --> 00:04:42.166
<b>This is</b>

71
00:04:42.166 --> 00:04:43.958
<b>manogataan.</b>

72
00:04:43.958 --> 00:04:48.208
<b>The mind's constant wandering.</b>

73
00:04:48.208 --> 00:04:56.458
<b>Creating countless beautiful/ugly/worrying/</b>
<b>joyful images.</b>

74
00:04:56.458 --> 00:04:57.250
<b>But</b>

75
00:04:57.250 --> 00:05:00.083
<b>the bigger dilemma is that</b>

76
00:05:00.083 --> 00:05:04.041
<b>if the mind isn't controlled,</b>

77
00:05:04.041 --> 00:05:10.375
<b>this process continues endlessly throughout life.</b>

78
00:05:10.375 --> 00:05:11.458
<b>always seeking a better</b>

79
00:05:11.458 --> 00:05:17.833
<b>object, a better situation, a better person than </b>
<b>the present one. The mind will endlessly search</b>

80
00:05:17.833 --> 00:05:20.708
<b>Consider this</b>

81
00:05:20.708 --> 00:05:23.750
<b>you like others,</b>

82
00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:27.250
<b>but don't like yourself.</b>

83
00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:30.958
<b>Others think you have everything,</b>

84
00:05:30.958 --> 00:05:34.666
<b>but you're not satisfied.</b>

85
00:05:34.666 --> 00:05:36.333
<b>And conversely...</b>

86
00:05:36.333 --> 00:05:38.833
<b>you like yourself,</b>

87
00:05:38.833 --> 00:05:41.708
<b>you're content with life.</b>

88
00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:48.041
<b>Then external objects/people have no impact.</b>

89
00:05:48.041 --> 00:05:50.166
<b>Manogataan.</b>

90
00:05:50.166 --> 00:05:52.000
<b>Mind's wandering.</b>

91
00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:55.666
<b>Wandering happens outside home, right?</b>

92
00:05:55.666 --> 00:05:59.208
<b>One who has come home </b>
<b>isn't wandering anymore.</b>

93
00:05:59.208 --> 00:06:00.625
<b>Similarly,</b>

94
00:06:00.625 --> 00:06:08.041
<b>when the mind returns not outward</b>
<b>but to its own home, returns within,</b>

95
00:06:08.041 --> 00:06:12.500
<b>there's no greater joy elsewhere.</b>

96
00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:15.750
<b>Continue on this spiritual journey,</b>

97
00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:21.041
<b>it will lead you home.</b>

98
00:06:21.041 --> 00:06:22.791
<b>During this journey,</b>

99
00:06:22.791 --> 00:06:26.833
<b>the mind won't be completely controlled,</b>

100
00:06:26.833 --> 00:06:28.000
<b>but</b>

101
00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:32.291
<b>when desire arises for any object/situation,</b>

102
00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:36.375
<b>just ask this question:</b>

103
00:06:36.375 --> 00:06:38.875
<b>Is this necessary for me?</b>

104
00:06:38.875 --> 00:06:44.875
<b>Or is the mind just wandering </b>
<b>toward momentary pleasure?</b>

105
00:06:49.916 --> 00:06:52.416
<b>Nurturing family,</b>

106
00:06:52.416 --> 00:06:54.500
<b>seeing them happy,</b>

107
00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:57.208
<b>their smiling faces,</b>

108
00:06:57.208 --> 00:06:58.500
<b>this is</b>

109
00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:02.333
<b>a very joyful experience.</b>

110
00:07:02.333 --> 00:07:03.666
<b>However,</b>

111
00:07:03.666 --> 00:07:15.250
<b>sometimes you make the mistake of making their </b>
<b>happiness dependent on fulfilling every little desire.</b>

112
00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:17.583
<b>As soon as a desire is expressed,</b>

113
00:07:17.583 --> 00:07:22.625
<b>you rush to acquire those things,</b>

114
00:07:22.625 --> 00:07:25.958
<b>quickly present them.</b>

115
00:07:25.958 --> 00:07:33.375
<b>The dilemma here is that if you haven't</b>
<b>thought about this logically,</b>

116
00:07:33.375 --> 00:07:36.625
<b>it becomes a cycle.</b>

117
00:07:36.625 --> 00:07:42.333
<b>A cycle of desires/expectations </b>
<b>and their fulfillment.</b>

118
00:07:42.333 --> 00:07:48.458
<b>And it's impossible to keep running </b>
<b>on this cycle continuously.</b>

119
00:07:48.458 --> 00:07:53.125
<b>Whether you're wealthy or not doesn't matter.</b>

120
00:07:53.125 --> 00:07:57.333
<b>This is also about control and balance,</b>

121
00:07:57.333 --> 00:07:59.583
<b>which is necessary.</b>

122
00:07:59.583 --> 00:08:02.083
<b>Keep two things in mind:</b>

123
00:08:02.083 --> 00:08:03.041
<b>First</b>

124
00:08:03.041 --> 00:08:06.958
<b>– Know the difference between </b>
<b>needs and expectations.</b>

125
00:08:06.958 --> 00:08:11.083
<b>Fulfilling needs is your responsibility.</b>

126
00:08:11.083 --> 00:08:11.875
<b>But</b>

127
00:08:11.875 --> 00:08:20.041
<b>trying to fulfill all expectations is neither good </b>
<b>for you nor family members.</b>

128
00:08:20.041 --> 00:08:23.000
<b>Because this is an endless process.</b>

129
00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:27.208
<b>This is manogataan, </b>
<b>the game of the wandering mind.</b>

130
00:08:27.208 --> 00:08:31.583
<b>Today this, tomorrow that.</b>

131
00:08:31.583 --> 00:08:33.000
<b>Second</b>

132
00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:36.958
<b>– You must also set a good example.</b>

133
00:08:36.958 --> 00:08:46.458
<b>Are you too setting a wrong example </b>
<b>by considering all mind's cravings important?</b>

134
00:08:46.458 --> 00:08:51.166
<b>This process must be implemented </b>
<b>gradually in the family.</b>

135
00:08:51.166 --> 00:08:53.041
<b>How nice it</b>

136
00:08:53.041 --> 00:08:55.500
<b>would be if when an aspiration arises,</b>

137
00:08:55.500 --> 00:09:03.083
<b>everyone considers whether </b>
<b>this is a need or mind's desire.</b>

138
00:09:03.083 --> 00:09:04.875
<b>And if it's a desire,</b>

139
00:09:04.875 --> 00:09:07.541
<b>is it momentary?</b>

140
00:09:07.541 --> 00:09:12.041
<b>Is it just imitating others?</b>

141
00:09:12.041 --> 00:09:13.875
<b>This thought process</b>

142
00:09:13.875 --> 00:09:16.166
<b>will not only create balance</b>

143
00:09:16.166 --> 00:09:23.958
<b>but also develop a sense of responsibility </b>
<b>in the family, especially in children.</b>

144
00:09:28.958 --> 00:09:30.708
<b>In an organization,</b>

145
00:09:30.708 --> 00:09:33.166
<b>comparative work style</b>

146
00:09:33.166 --> 00:09:37.916
<b>can certainly be a source</b>
<b>of motivation and energy.</b>

147
00:09:37.916 --> 00:09:39.041
<b>However,</b>

148
00:09:39.041 --> 00:09:45.583
<b>it sometimes takes the form </b>
<b>of unhealthy competition.</b>

149
00:09:45.583 --> 00:09:47.083
<b>In this situation,</b>

150
00:09:47.083 --> 00:09:51.041
<b>some people rather than</b>
<b>improving their own work,</b>

151
00:09:51.041 --> 00:09:56.416
<b>become more interested in others' failure.</b>

152
00:09:56.416 --> 00:09:58.916
<b>Why does this happen?</b>

153
00:09:58.916 --> 00:10:05.458
<b>One fundamental reason is dissatisfaction.</b>

154
00:10:05.458 --> 00:10:12.083
<b>If someone feels their capabilities </b>
<b>aren't being fully utilized,</b>

155
00:10:12.083 --> 00:10:17.041
<b>this dissatisfaction can arise.</b>

156
00:10:17.041 --> 00:10:21.666
<b>In such situations, people become negative,</b>

157
00:10:21.666 --> 00:10:27.541
<b>taking pleasure in other’s failure</b>

158
00:10:27.541 --> 00:10:34.291
<b>because they feel they could have </b>
<b>done better than the other person.</b>

159
00:10:34.291 --> 00:10:45.583
<b>But the dilemma is that this might </b>
<b>all be just the person's imagination.</b>

160
00:10:45.583 --> 00:10:47.958
<b>In an imaginary world,</b>

161
00:10:47.958 --> 00:10:52.375
<b>everyone is the best.</b>

162
00:10:52.375 --> 00:10:54.583
<b>So what should be done?</b>

163
00:10:54.583 --> 00:11:00.625
<b>If you're in a leadership position,</b>
<b>keep these things in mind:</b>

164
00:11:00.625 --> 00:11:02.083
<b>First</b>

165
00:11:02.083 --> 00:11:06.583
<b>Rejecting, dismissing this </b>
<b>thinking would be a mistake,</b>

166
00:11:06.583 --> 00:11:12.166
<b>this is a natural reaction of a dissatisfied person.</b>

167
00:11:12.166 --> 00:11:13.333
<b>Second</b>

168
00:11:13.333 --> 00:11:15.000
<b>Communication</b>

169
00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:22.458
<b>through conversation you can encourage </b>
<b>someone, help them understand.</b>

170
00:11:22.458 --> 00:11:23.791
<b>Third</b>

171
00:11:23.791 --> 00:11:24.791
<b>Challenges.</b>

172
00:11:24.791 --> 00:11:26.500
<b>Not competition,</b>

173
00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:28.500
<b>but personal challenges.</b>

174
00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:36.208
<b>Where no one is ahead/behind, everyone </b>
<b>is striving toward their own given goal.</b>

175
00:11:36.208 --> 00:11:39.083
<b>This reduces unhealthy competition</b>

176
00:11:39.083 --> 00:11:45.833
<b>and also helps you assess people's capabilities.</b>

177
00:11:45.833 --> 00:11:50.458
<b>Here the conversation won't be </b>
<b>about imaginary competition,</b>

178
00:11:50.458 --> 00:11:51.333
<b>but</b>

179
00:11:51.333 --> 00:11:55.958
<b>about real and personal challenges.</b>

180
00:11:55.958 --> 00:12:02.125
<b>The question of others being </b>
<b>good or bad doesn't arise.</b>

181
00:12:02.125 --> 00:12:06.375
<b>The difference between imagination </b>
<b>and reality becomes clear.</b>

182
00:12:06.375 --> 00:12:10.375
<b>You might learn something new,</b>

183
00:12:10.375 --> 00:12:16.291
<b>or be able to calmly understand the person.</b>

